WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.130
{Chapter 06}

00:10.950 --> 00:12.030
Takumi.

00:25.880 --> 00:26.880
What?

00:29.680 --> 00:30.890
Come here!

00:32.800 --> 00:34.390
Grab me!

00:34.930 --> 00:36.390
Grab me,

00:38.440 --> 00:40.190
and never let me go!

00:44.980 --> 00:49.070
You'd better not pick anything over me!

00:56.660 --> 00:58.660
You'd better not.

01:20.060 --> 01:25.610
I've heard it said so many times

01:26.320 --> 01:32.530
How it's not going to work out

01:33.490 --> 01:39.000
That nothing will change

01:39.330 --> 01:45.500
Even if I pretended not to listen

01:45.960 --> 01:49.339
I knew it all

01:49.340 --> 01:52.509
I learned this from you

01:52.510 --> 02:00.510
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:01.890 --> 02:08.479
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

02:08.480 --> 02:15.409
The quiet melodies push me forward

02:15.410 --> 02:21.909
Because the sky is so vast and free

02:21.910 --> 02:29.550
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

02:48.400 --> 02:50.150
Come on, Kadowaki. Let's go.

02:55.240 --> 02:58.660
Hey, you got a call
from Kaionji, didn't you?

02:59.160 --> 03:00.659
What did he say?

03:00.660 --> 03:03.329
Nothing that has anything to do with you.

03:03.330 --> 03:05.039
It was about the game, wasn't it?

03:05.040 --> 03:07.330
How is that not related to me?

03:08.290 --> 03:09.540
Don't get carried away.

03:10.420 --> 03:14.339
I can't believe you can say that after
how little you're thinking about the game.

03:14.340 --> 03:18.260
The only thing on your mind is Harada.

03:18.800 --> 03:24.809
Have you even given a single thought to how
we're going to win the game or who to start?

03:24.810 --> 03:26.690
Yeah, but...

03:27.560 --> 03:30.519
It has nothing to do with you.

03:30.520 --> 03:35.319
Shun, I've noticed that you've
become more short-tempered lately.

03:35.320 --> 03:36.280
Really?

03:36.280 --> 03:37.280
Yeah.

03:37.281 --> 03:40.780
You used to get mad at me
all the time when we were little.

03:41.660 --> 03:43.830
Like when I was lagging behind.

03:44.580 --> 03:48.749
Whoa, let's save the reminiscing
for after we're old and bald.

03:48.750 --> 03:50.339
It's good.

03:50.340 --> 03:54.089
You seem more like the
real you when you're angry.

03:54.090 --> 03:55.090
I like it.

03:57.590 --> 03:59.429
Thanks.

03:59.430 --> 04:04.100
That reminds me,
you've always been a bit of a masochist.

04:05.930 --> 04:07.599
Why don't you wipe your sweat off?

04:07.600 --> 04:08.770
Oh, yeah.

04:20.240 --> 04:23.659
You need to work on your abs, Shuugo.

04:23.660 --> 04:24.950
What the hell?

04:25.250 --> 04:27.499
I'm just paying you back for the other day.

04:27.500 --> 04:29.709
Now we're even.

04:29.710 --> 04:30.830
See you.

04:31.710 --> 04:33.209
Hold on!

04:33.210 --> 04:36.300
What the hell is your problem?!

04:38.220 --> 04:41.050
You keep acting like you know me.

04:42.970 --> 04:44.680
What do you mean by the "real" me?

04:45.560 --> 04:47.979
Why would you know what that is?

04:47.980 --> 04:53.730
I've never once shown you the real me.

04:55.360 --> 04:56.650
Remember that.

04:59.490 --> 05:00.739
Shuugo.

05:00.740 --> 05:03.909
I hate you.

05:03.910 --> 05:06.409
I couldn't stand you.

05:06.410 --> 05:10.290
I kept wishing you'd just
go away and disappear.

05:11.000 --> 05:12.250
Since forever.

05:13.420 --> 05:15.339
It's not your fault.

05:15.340 --> 05:17.760
But what was I supposed to do?

05:18.260 --> 05:20.630
I just hate you too much.

05:23.050 --> 05:24.220
Sorry.

06:20.780 --> 06:22.530
Yokote Baseball Park

06:22.531 --> 06:24.280
Yokote Baseball Park

06:40.760 --> 06:44.049
Omizu! You're seriously starting Hagi?

06:44.050 --> 06:45.050
Yeah.

06:45.340 --> 06:46.889
Why not me?

06:46.890 --> 06:48.469
Because it's dangerous.

06:48.470 --> 06:49.680
Dangerous?

06:50.390 --> 06:52.389
You saying they'd hit off of me?

06:52.390 --> 06:53.560
Enomoto.

06:54.060 --> 06:59.570
You don't have to tell me how good
of a pitcher you are. I already know.

07:00.610 --> 07:03.569
I've been watching your back
on the field this whole time.

07:03.570 --> 07:05.320
Then why?

07:06.030 --> 07:07.239
Don't make me say it.

07:07.240 --> 07:08.240
Say what?

07:11.620 --> 07:14.330
You hurt your shoulder, didn't you?

07:16.000 --> 07:19.710
You've been a bit off since nationals.

07:20.710 --> 07:23.839
I didn't tell anybody about
that. How did you know?

07:23.840 --> 07:25.590
I already told you.

07:25.880 --> 07:28.009
I'm always behind you.

07:28.010 --> 07:29.969
I've been watching your
back this whole time.

07:29.970 --> 07:31.389
It's all better now, though.

07:31.390 --> 07:32.849
Give it up.

07:32.850 --> 07:35.059
It won't work on him.

07:35.060 --> 07:37.850
Omizu, just give it to him straight.

07:38.190 --> 07:40.650
Enomoto's not going
to be satisfied otherwise.

07:42.610 --> 07:43.610
Look.

07:44.610 --> 07:47.239
That's Nitta East's pitcher.

07:47.240 --> 07:49.370
Can you really compete with him?

07:50.160 --> 07:54.539
They've been practicing with the
assumption that you'd be playing.

07:54.540 --> 07:57.369
They've been using him as your stand-in.

07:57.370 --> 08:00.460
They're gonna be good against fast pitches.

08:02.710 --> 08:05.339
You're gonna keep
pitching in high school, right?

08:05.340 --> 08:07.010
Don't push yourself here.

08:09.260 --> 08:11.469
I guess I'll go stand in the coach's box.

08:11.470 --> 08:12.640
Omizu.

08:12.930 --> 08:15.889
How did you know about Enomoto's shoulder?

08:15.890 --> 08:17.599
I'm a shortstop.

08:17.600 --> 08:20.649
I know my pitcher's condition
like the back of my hand.

08:20.650 --> 08:23.359
I didn't notice at all.

08:23.360 --> 08:26.819
Don't underestimate Nitta East, Karaki.

08:26.820 --> 08:28.950
Mizugaki!

08:32.990 --> 08:34.119
'Sup!

08:34.120 --> 08:35.329
Kurinosuke!

08:35.330 --> 08:37.579
Why are you here?

08:37.580 --> 08:41.129
What do you mean,
why? I play for Nitta East.

08:41.130 --> 08:42.419
You missed me, didn't you?

08:42.420 --> 08:43.589
Don't be stupid.

08:43.590 --> 08:46.209
You're the last person I wanted to see.

08:46.210 --> 08:48.340
Oh, don't be like that.

08:48.670 --> 08:51.510
I came all this way to trade lineups.

08:52.260 --> 08:53.600
Oh, whatever.

08:54.680 --> 08:56.059
Hey, Kurinosuke.

08:56.060 --> 08:57.099
Yeah, yeah, yeah?

08:57.100 --> 08:59.389
One "yeah" is enough.

08:59.390 --> 09:01.480
How's your team holding up?

09:01.770 --> 09:03.979
I'm doing great.

09:03.980 --> 09:07.149
Nobody's asking how you are!
I'm talking about your battery.

09:07.150 --> 09:09.989
Oh, those two.

09:09.990 --> 09:11.699
Hard to say.

09:11.700 --> 09:13.990
I don't think they're doing too hot.

09:14.660 --> 09:18.000
Harada's still got some
ball-control issues.

09:18.620 --> 09:22.209
Maybe I should've played catcher.

09:22.210 --> 09:23.500
Yoshisada!

09:23.880 --> 09:26.170
Stop blabbing to the enemy!

09:28.970 --> 09:30.549
I'm Nonomura.

09:30.550 --> 09:32.010
I look forward to our game.

09:34.430 --> 09:35.889
Thank you.

09:35.890 --> 09:38.349
So you're the future captain, huh?

09:38.350 --> 09:39.519
Yes.

09:39.520 --> 09:40.889
I thought so.

09:40.890 --> 09:42.349
You can tell?

09:42.350 --> 09:43.730
Of course.

09:44.560 --> 09:49.899
Must be hard for a team to come
together with a battery like that.

09:49.900 --> 09:52.779
Are you jealous, Mizugaki?

09:52.780 --> 09:54.030
What did you say?

09:54.450 --> 09:58.410
Having a battery like them on your team

09:58.870 --> 10:00.369
is really fun.

10:00.370 --> 10:01.540
Excuse us.

10:04.500 --> 10:05.539
Karaki.

10:05.540 --> 10:08.379
We're up now. Hit some
balls for fielding practice.

10:08.380 --> 10:09.380
All right.

10:11.090 --> 10:13.050
I didn't notice either.

10:13.680 --> 10:15.140
Notice what?

10:16.010 --> 10:17.430
Enomoto's shoulder.

10:18.350 --> 10:20.349
You don't need to.

10:20.350 --> 10:22.690
Actually, not noticing
is the kind thing to do.

10:23.390 --> 10:26.440
I wouldn't have said anything if
we weren't facing the princess.

10:26.860 --> 10:29.440
It's not Harada's fault.

10:29.730 --> 10:30.859
I know.

10:30.860 --> 10:33.150
He's just getting up on
that mound and pitching.

10:33.820 --> 10:37.450
He doesn't mean to make
everyone around him feel cornered.

10:38.200 --> 10:41.450
Those are the ones to look out for.

10:43.920 --> 10:45.460
I think that's enough.

10:46.210 --> 10:47.379
What?

10:47.380 --> 10:49.710
I think that's enough about Harada.

10:50.340 --> 10:53.880
This game never would've
happened if it weren't for you.

10:58.350 --> 11:02.519
I've been watching you
from behind all this time.

11:02.520 --> 11:03.979
Well, you play left field.

11:03.980 --> 11:05.900
That's not altogether surprising.

11:07.270 --> 11:09.019
I mean, since we were kids.

11:09.020 --> 11:10.730
It's got nothing to do with baseball.

11:11.650 --> 11:12.650
Let's go.

11:15.700 --> 11:16.910
Mr. Atou.

11:17.950 --> 11:19.619
Mr. Tomura!

11:19.620 --> 11:21.449
It's been a long time.

11:21.450 --> 11:22.909
Are you here to watch?

11:22.910 --> 11:24.500
Watch?

11:24.960 --> 11:27.789
That's one way of putting it.

11:27.790 --> 11:33.009
I've taken this opportunity to
observe your team practice.

11:33.010 --> 11:33.920
Right.

11:33.921 --> 11:39.599
Kadowaki asked me some time ago
to arrange a game with your school.

11:39.600 --> 11:42.519
He said he wanted to face
off against Nitta's pitcher.

11:42.520 --> 11:46.309
I ignored him, telling him
we didn't have the time.

11:46.310 --> 11:47.519
That's only natural.

11:47.520 --> 11:49.270
I would've done the same.

11:49.650 --> 11:53.189
I suspect the one throwing
earlier was that pitcher?

11:53.190 --> 11:54.609
His name is Harada.

11:54.610 --> 11:55.989
And the catcher?

11:55.990 --> 11:57.779
He's Nagakura.

11:57.780 --> 11:59.910
I hear they're only juniors.

12:00.200 --> 12:01.200
Yes.

12:01.410 --> 12:05.659
Nitta East will be in the prefectural
tournament this year, won't they?

12:05.660 --> 12:06.790
Definitely.

12:07.120 --> 12:13.800
The reason Mizugaki started Jouno and Hagi was
probably because he took the tournament into account.

12:15.300 --> 12:20.799
He wanted to see Nitta East's
new battery with his own eyes.

12:20.800 --> 12:24.929
I wouldn't put that past him.

12:24.930 --> 12:26.849
Well, I'm not wasting this opportunity.

12:26.850 --> 12:30.859
I'll be keeping a close eye on
this game as Yokote's coach.

12:30.860 --> 12:34.150
It seems that you guys are
real contenders this year.

12:35.150 --> 12:36.690
Please be gentle.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.040
Makoto.

12:51.500 --> 12:52.590
Coach.

12:53.250 --> 12:55.089
You've come to watch?

12:55.090 --> 12:57.379
This one kept pestering me.

12:57.380 --> 12:59.839
He really wants to
watch his brother's game.

12:59.840 --> 13:02.350
Seiha, wasn't it?

13:02.970 --> 13:04.850
You've come to cheer
with your grandpa, huh?

13:05.430 --> 13:07.059
Not to cheer.

13:07.060 --> 13:08.100
I came to watch.

13:09.600 --> 13:11.019
Are you here to cheer them on, mister?

13:11.020 --> 13:12.480
I suppose so.

13:13.310 --> 13:14.609
You suppose?

13:14.610 --> 13:17.610
Why is the coach in the stands, anyway?

13:21.160 --> 13:24.409
You should be down there in the dugout.

13:24.410 --> 13:26.240
It's a little complicated.

13:26.540 --> 13:29.289
Today is just a game between the kids.

13:29.290 --> 13:30.290
I see.

13:32.040 --> 13:33.040
Coach.

13:35.540 --> 13:37.210
These are my students.

13:37.760 --> 13:40.009
I look forward to seeing them play.

13:40.010 --> 13:42.389
But could you stop calling me "Coach"?

13:42.390 --> 13:45.639
I'm just an old man now.

13:45.640 --> 13:50.099
No, you will always be Coach to us.

13:50.100 --> 13:52.560
Are you Mr. Ioka?

13:53.440 --> 13:55.939
The former coach of Nitta High School?

13:55.940 --> 13:57.269
That's right.

13:57.270 --> 13:58.859
Oh, hello.

13:58.860 --> 14:01.030
I'm honored to meet you.

14:01.650 --> 14:03.530
Would you mind if I shook your hand?

14:07.660 --> 14:13.039
Every time Nitta High School went
to nationals, I was glued to the TV.

14:13.040 --> 14:16.459
I didn't realize you
liked baseball, Principal.

14:16.460 --> 14:17.799
I love baseball.

14:17.800 --> 14:20.879
I might not be able to play,
but I do enjoy watching it.

14:20.880 --> 14:23.549
I was never much of an athlete.

14:23.550 --> 14:25.050
I was quite frail.

14:25.590 --> 14:28.810
I was so jealous of all
the good baseball players.

14:29.390 --> 14:30.390
You're wrong.

14:32.350 --> 14:33.769
You're wrong, mister.

14:33.770 --> 14:34.770
Huh?

14:35.020 --> 14:36.689
What am I wrong about?

14:36.690 --> 14:41.440
Even if you're bad at gym or have a
frail body, you can still play baseball.

14:42.780 --> 14:44.950
You can if you really love it.

14:45.450 --> 14:48.830
I'm gonna play baseball
and beat my brother.

14:49.450 --> 14:50.579
Brother?

14:50.580 --> 14:53.210
Well, you'd better watch
your brother closely.

14:53.580 --> 14:56.420
Watch and see what kind of
baseball he and his team plays.

14:59.750 --> 15:01.210
Isn't this fun?

15:13.060 --> 15:14.270
Cherry blossoms.

15:15.140 --> 15:16.480
Cherry blossoms?

15:17.020 --> 15:19.230
These cherry blossoms
will produce cherries.

15:23.240 --> 15:25.400
They blossom earlier than the others.

15:28.620 --> 15:30.120
Line up!

15:38.580 --> 15:40.090
Let's have a good game!

15:48.260 --> 15:49.220
Harada.

15:49.220 --> 15:50.220
Yes?

15:50.390 --> 15:51.640
It's finally time.

15:52.560 --> 15:53.390
Yes.

15:53.391 --> 15:55.979
I've been waiting for you for a long time.

15:55.980 --> 15:57.650
Too long.

16:14.410 --> 16:15.410
Play ball!

16:21.670 --> 16:22.710
Ball.

16:33.930 --> 16:35.180
Strike.

16:35.930 --> 16:37.180
Strike.

16:39.020 --> 16:40.020
Ball.

16:48.070 --> 16:49.070
Out.

17:13.890 --> 17:16.640
It's been a while, boy.

17:17.020 --> 17:19.640
I see you're batting third, Mizugaki.

17:20.350 --> 17:23.650
I've always wanted the
chance to bat before Shuugo.

17:24.400 --> 17:27.650
You're not going to crumble
like you did last time, are you?

17:28.820 --> 17:29.820
Of course not.

17:31.160 --> 17:33.450
My, haven't we gotten brash.

17:34.580 --> 17:38.660
You would've been cuter if
you were still that same little boy.

17:54.970 --> 17:56.100
Out.

17:56.680 --> 17:57.680
Damn it!

18:00.850 --> 18:02.100
Nice pitching.

18:08.150 --> 18:09.150
It got through!

18:09.690 --> 18:11.989
You're going to get to bat, Kaionji.

18:11.990 --> 18:12.990
Yeah.

18:15.950 --> 18:18.119
Hagi's pitches tend to
rise at the start of the game.

18:18.120 --> 18:19.290
Be careful.

18:20.620 --> 18:21.790
Takatsuki.

18:22.580 --> 18:24.630
Do you want to pitch?

18:25.540 --> 18:27.839
I'm sorry. Forget it.

18:27.840 --> 18:30.299
I mean, I'm not real particular about it.

18:30.300 --> 18:31.300
I see.

18:31.301 --> 18:34.510
I mean, the mound's a small place.

18:35.430 --> 18:37.890
I like being out in the field.

18:40.140 --> 18:44.939
The diamond, the outfield, I love it all.

18:44.940 --> 18:46.400
Right, Harada?

18:46.690 --> 18:48.979
The mound's small, isn't it?

18:48.980 --> 18:51.899
I've never felt that way before.

18:51.900 --> 18:54.569
You don't see it that way, huh?

18:54.570 --> 18:55.570
I don't.

18:58.700 --> 19:00.290
Two outs, huh?

19:01.250 --> 19:03.540
It's nice to see you again, Kaionji.

19:03.870 --> 19:05.289
Jouno, wasn't it?

19:05.290 --> 19:06.080
Yes.

19:06.081 --> 19:07.499
I've been looking forward to this.

19:07.500 --> 19:08.500
I see.

19:10.710 --> 19:12.050
Strike.

19:23.680 --> 19:24.770
Out!

19:27.190 --> 19:28.309
Damn it!

19:28.310 --> 19:32.899
Our center fielder Taoka's got
the strongest arm in the country.

19:32.900 --> 19:34.070
I'll keep that in mind.

19:34.400 --> 19:37.529
I'll just have to hit it
over his head next time.

19:37.530 --> 19:39.489
All we need is one point to win, after all.

19:39.490 --> 19:42.790
That's some big talk considering that
panicked phone call you made to me.

19:44.830 --> 19:46.080
Hey, Mizugaki.

19:47.330 --> 19:50.380
Baseball's real fun, isn't it?

19:53.880 --> 19:55.759
Yokote doesn't disappoint.

19:55.760 --> 19:56.760
Yeah.

20:01.310 --> 20:02.970
Here, partner.

20:05.810 --> 20:07.599
Let's go, Takumi.

20:07.600 --> 20:10.149
It's been a long wait, hasn't it, Shuugo?

20:10.150 --> 20:11.269
Yeah.

20:11.270 --> 20:12.480
Go get 'em.

20:20.820 --> 20:21.950
Harada.

20:32.500 --> 20:34.880
Kadowaki Shuugo.

20:50.230 --> 20:51.940
That's what I'm talking about.

21:15.670 --> 21:16.670
Takumi!

21:23.350 --> 21:27.895
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:27.896 --> 21:32.439
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:32.440 --> 21:37.925
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:37.926 --> 21:43.410
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:45.990 --> 21:50.475
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:50.476 --> 21:54.959
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:54.960 --> 21:59.965
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

21:59.966 --> 22:04.969
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

22:04.970 --> 22:09.495
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

22:09.496 --> 22:14.019
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

22:14.020 --> 22:15.400
- I love you
- I love you

22:15.403 --> 22:19.235
That was probably the day before eternity

22:19.236 --> 22:23.069
That was probably the day before eternity

22:23.070 --> 22:25.300
If spring comes tomorrow

22:25.301 --> 22:27.529
If spring comes tomorrow

22:27.530 --> 22:29.825
I will go to meet you

22:29.826 --> 22:32.119
I will go to meet you

22:32.120 --> 22:34.355
When the rain turns to sunshine

22:34.356 --> 22:36.589
When the rain turns to sunshine

22:36.590 --> 22:38.880
Will you remember where to stop?

22:38.881 --> 22:41.170
Will you remember where to stop?
